[{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-872"
  :itonami.blueprint/name "Residential Care Activities for Mental Retardation, Mental Health and Substance Abuse"
  :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev4 "872"
  :itonami.blueprint/domain :services/residential-care-mental-health-substance-abuse
  :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
  :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:dignity-and-autonomy :person-centered-care :family-engagement :safety-and-wellbeing :recovery-and-rehabilitation]
  :itonami.blueprint/governor :mhscare-governor
  :itonami.blueprint/robotics false
  :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger]
  :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
  :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
  :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
  "MhsCareAdvisor ⊣ MhsCareGovernor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
  (langgraph.graph, mhscare.operation/build), append-only audit ledger
  (mhscare.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore -- already
  genuinely wired pre-fix, not dead code). Fixes two real bugs, not a
  redesign: (1) `deps.edn` declared NO `langgraph` dependency
  anywhere -- worse than the usual `:dev`-only-override gap elsewhere
  in this fleet -- and `operation.cljc`'s `run-proposal` was a plain
  nested-`if`/`let` pipeline whose own comment admitted \"Simple
  workflow runner for testing (not using langgraph-clj StateGraph
  machinery yet)\"; this maturity field claimed `:implemented` despite
  that being false. (2) `run-proposal` never actually called its own
  `intake-node` (`intake-state` set `:decision :pending`, so the
  dead-code check `(if (= (:decision state) :hold) ...)` never fired),
  so required-field validation never ran on any real call path.  Now:
  a genuinely compiled StateGraph (`:intake -+-> :advise -> :govern ->
  :decide -+-> :commit / :escalate -> :request-approval -+-> :commit /
  :hold` / `+-> :hold`) with `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` +
  in-memory checkpointer for real human-in-the-loop resume -- this
  resume path is GENUINELY NEW: the pre-fix `escalate-node` was a dead
  end (logged `:proposal-escalated` and stopped; no mechanism anywhere
  in this repo let an escalated proposal ever be approved-and-
  committed or rejected-and-held). The Governor (three HARD, permanent
  checks: resident-unverified, effect-not-propose, scope-excluded
  medication/clinical/care-plan/restraint/guardianship/disciplinary/
  end-of-life/safety-authority content) and rollout phase gate were
  already real logic; both preserved unchanged, only wired into real
  graph nodes. Five closed-allowlist ops (`:log-resident-note` /
  `:schedule-family-or-guardian-visit` / `:coordinate-supply-request` /
  `:schedule-staff-shift-proposal` / `:flag-safety-concern`), all
  `:effect :propose` only. `:flag-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to
  a human clinician via the compiled graph's `:request-approval` node,
  proven by `test/mhscare/operation_test.kotoba` exercising commit /
  hard-hold (unverified resident) / invalid-request-hold-at-intake /
  phase-escalate / escalate-approve / escalate-reject through the REAL
  compiled graph end to end, plus a `clojure -X:run` demo runner
  producing real ledger entries. 45 tests / 124 assertions green
  (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0 errors (`clojure -M:lint`)."
  :db/id -1}]
